## Onion Architecture

```
cmd/
└── main.go                  ← entry point, wires dependencies

internal/
├── config/config.go           ← reads env
├── middleware/                 ← auth, rate limiting
├── errors/app_error.go         ← error types and helpers
├── shared/                     ← database, cache, health
│   ├── database/
│   ├── cache/
│   └── health/
├── domain/                     ← innermost layer — entities, interfaces, domain logic
│   └── <module>/
│       ├── entity.go           ← domain entity struct
│       ├── repository.go       ← repository interface (no impl)
│       └── service.go          ← pure domain logic
├── application/                ← use cases, DTOs — orchestrates domain
│   └── <module>/
│       ├── usecase.go          ← application use cases
│       └── dto.go              ← request/response DTOs
└── infrastructure/             ← outermost layer — adapts domain to framework
    ├── persistence/
    │   └── <module>_repository.go  ← implements domain.Repository
    └── handler/
        └── <module>_handler.go     ← HTTP handler (framework-specific)
```

**Dependency rule:** Inner layers (domain) never import outer layers (infrastructure).
Domain has zero framework imports. Infrastructure adapts domain interfaces to the framework.

